i know i seem really tough but i am  afraid of heights yeah  one thing i'm afraid of action heroes  and huge stars  might seem like they live their lives  with absolutely no fear  but it turns out that even the biggest  celebs aren't brave about  everything that's right a ton of actors  are stricken with some very serious  phobias  but the best ones never let that stand  in the way of their dream job  even if their dream job is deep  underwater or  at the top of a terrifyingly tall  building these amazing actors pushed  through their phobias and conquered them  for their most  iconic roles i'm really glad that i went  through the process of auditioning  because i felt like okay  i really i earned this now you might  think that someone who has been an  a-list celebrity since they were 9 years  old like  emma watson fears nothing but when it  came time to audition for belle in  beauty and the beast  one huge fear almost made her throw in  the towel  singing emma hadn't sung since she was  12  and was absolutely terrified of having  to sing in front of anyone  let alone millions and millions of fans  she  even hated doing karaoke that was mildly  terrifying  but knowing that her dream job was on  the line she leaned into her fear  challenged herself and completely  conquered you know i wish i could say it  was  a little fluffy to do but it was that  intense if we already had a fear of  tight enclosed spaces  we probably wouldn't jump at the chance  to make a movie about being buried alive  but that's exactly what ryan reynolds  did in 2010's buried  if you don't remember the entire movie  takes place inside a sealed coffin  with reynolds trapped inside during the  shoot he has said that he actually had  safe words that he would shout to be  pulled out if he needed it  but the majority spanish-speaking crew  didn't always understand  and would leave him in there during a  panic attack the shoot was so rough that  he says he was both physically  and emotionally changed after filming  finished and the last day of shooting  was  uh was unlike anything i've ever  experienced in my life  even though anthony mackey's marvel  character falcon does  a lot of flying it turns out that the  actor actually has one huge fear of his  own  heights yup that means that every time  he had to soar through the air  or leap off of a tall building he was  totally terrified  every single time one time he even had  to leap off of a bridge and land  right on top of a car sure he had wires  to make sure he lived through the  experience  but it definitely wasn't easy oh yeah i  mean like we learned horse riding i  don't know if you've done it before  but yeah robert pattinson had to  interact with a lot of animals for the  2011 film  water for elephants but it wasn't the  giant elephants that made him nervous  it was the horses it turns out that the  actor has a long-standing fear of horses  and one scene in particular freaked him  out the most  in it he had to get knocked over by a  full-grown stallion  and he did not have a good time on set  that day  terrified of riding rusty i hate it  apparently fear of horses runs in the  twilight family  because rob's co-star kristen stewart  also hates being around the four-legged  giants  during snow white and the huntsman she  knew that she was going to have to learn  to ride  and was completely terrified at the  thought even though she took lessons and  worked with some of the best trainers in  the world  she never really got over her fear and  said that she never wanted to ride again  after the shoot was over you're afraid  of heights  everyone's afraid of something shailene  woodley has said that she is very afraid  of heights  but actually loves leaning into her  fears in order to get the adrenaline  rush that she loves  so when it came time to climb to the top  of a ferris wheel in chicago for  divergent  she ran into the challenge head-on even  though she was freezing cold and very  uncomfortable  she loved 